.Dd November 12, 2026
.Dt ISSETUGID 3
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm issetugid ,
.Nm getauxval
.Nd query process security state
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In unistd.h
.Ft int
.Fn issetugid void
.Ft unsigned long
.Fn getauxval "unsigned long type"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn issetugid reports whether the process was started with elevated privilege. .Fn getauxval
reads the auxiliary vector supplied by the loader.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn issetugid returns 0 or 1. .Fn getauxval returns the value or 0 when the entry is absent.
.Sh ERRORS
.Fn getauxval sets .Er ENOENT when the entry is absent in some implementations; ravenlibc
returns 0.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libc 7
.Sh STANDARDS
BSD and glibc extension; ring 1 and ring 2.
.Sh CAVEATS
.Fn issetugid is always 0 because RavenBSD has no setuid exec path. AT_SECURE is always 0.
See H-7.
